        char b [3] [2];
        char *p = *b;
        for (i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
              for (j = 0; j < 3; j++) {
              *(p + 2*j + i) = a [i] [j];
              }
        }
}</code></pre> <br>What should be the contents of the array b at the end of the program?

Consider the C program given below. What does it print?<pre><code> #include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
int main ()
{
        int i, j;
        int a [8] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8};
        for(i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
             a[i] = a[i] + 1;
             i++;
        }
        i--;
        for (j = 7; j > 4; j--) {
              int i = j/2;
              a[i] = a[i] - 1;
        }
        printf ("%d, %d", i, a[i]);
}</code></pre>
